    {
      "rule_id": "CT-005",
      "fault_family": "cam_timing",
      "description": "VVT solenoid/actuator electrical fault: VVT solenoid coil resistance drift or actuator circuit fault. Gated on VVT_HISTORY range DTCs (P0010-P0023) \u2014 at least one VVT DTC must be present. No chemistry requirement \u2014 the electrical nature of the fault means chemistry may be NORMAL_OPERATION or ambiguous. OBD: fuel trims near zero (stft_b1 in_range [-5,5], ltft_b1 in_range [-5,5]) as SUGGESTIVE \u2014 solenoid drift causes marginal trim response, not the saturation pattern seen in ecu_fault. Confidence ceiling applied \u2014 sole DTC-primary rule in the cam_timing set. EXP-N023 (no DTC, no MAP, no RPM) is NOT covered and is documented as an Unplanned follow-up",
