      "rule_id": "CT-006",
      "fault_family": "cam_timing",
      "description": "TIMING_RETARDED chemistry with cam timing DTCs \u2014 Tier B gap closer: GASLab emits TIMING_RETARDED chemistry (elevated HC, depressed CO2, combustion phasing delayed) as a secondary effect of VVT phaser malfunction. Gated on VVT_HISTORY DTCs (P0011-P0024) \u2014 at least one VVT DTC must be present for this rule to evaluate. TIMING_RETARDED chemistry is SUGGESTIVE evidence, not a GATING condition \u2014 this rule competes with CT-002 on TIMING_RETARDED cases where VVT DTCs are also present. Confidence ceiling applied because TIMING_RETARDED chemistry is shared across 7 families and cam_timing is not the only consumer",
